  "extractionNotes": "ZUS page-1 note: the right to both benefits (sickness and maternity) was established and paid. ZUS insurance memo dated 2026-05-28 for the sickness claim 2026-02-02..2026-02-11: title 0590 with voluntary sickness from 2025-07-01, preceded without a gap by 0570 (2023-07-01..2025-06-30, ended by deregistration when the title changed); a sickness benefit 2026-02-12..2026-04-22 is listed as already paid or granted (type code redacted); contribution debt on 2026-02-02 = yes, repaid in full on 2026-05-21 (amount not stated, recorded as aboveThreshold); base below 60% of the forecast wage (last month 2026-02). The memo lists the declared bases 2025-02..2026-02 as one series across both codes; they are all attached to the current title (2026-02 is a partial-month base). Birth 2026-04-28; maternity follows the sickness after a 5-day gap, so the base is not recalculated. The ZAM (maternity 20 weeks + parental 32 weeks, full-length declaration ticked) is dated 2026-05-28, 30 days after the birth, so the 21-day deadline for the averaged rate was missed; rates are not printed (100% then 70% expected). A follow-up statement confirms maternity benefit from one title only. Payment came only after the debt was repaid, within the 6-month window."
